      "text": "Verified the portable-resume contracts at `c9e8c2d` from committed source, tests, and documentation:\n\n- Per file: **1 MiB = 1,048,576 bytes** for managed configuration and each canonical document read.\n- Aggregate: **8 MiB = 8,388,608 bytes** across one portable-resume canonical-context observation.\n- Always loaded: **16,000 JavaScript characters** of default context—not bytes, tokens, or a semantic-quality guarantee.\n\nStructural checkpoint validation only verifies canonical sections, uniqueness, and ordering. It does not prove freshness. Git checkpoint evidence is checked separately; `resume --check` must fail when that evidence is stale even if canonical files remain structurally valid. Behavioral continuity is a third, separate evidence layer.\n\nChecks actually run:\n\n- `npm run format:check`: passed; 64 files checked.\n- Focused `tests/continuity.test.mjs`: failed; 11 passed, 5 failed because temporary projects were reported outside a Git working tree.\n- Clean-diff check: passed.\n\nNo files were modified, staged, or committed."
